      "body": "Reference SharpNinja.Avalonia.RemoteControl.Server 0.7.4, with the CLI using matching published Protocol 0.7.4; restore/build is reproducible without sibling source paths through the supported package feeds.\nUse AddAvaloniaRemoteControl plus a DI IRemoteControlRootProvider for the live desktop MainWindow, and bind the host lifecycle to the classic-desktop lifetime.\nPreserve loopback/bearer/default-disabled behavior, deny-by-default action/frame gates and compatible central Avalonia/Grpc dependency constraints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- **ac-01**: Reference SharpNinja.Avalonia.RemoteControl.Server 0.7.4, with the CLI using matching published Protocol 0.7.4; restore/build is reproducible without sibling source paths through the supported package feeds.\n- **ac-02**: Use AddAvaloniaRemoteControl plus a DI IRemoteControlRootProvider for the live desktop MainWindow, and bind the host lifecycle to the classic-desktop lifetime.\n- **ac-03**: Preserve loopback/bearer/default-disabled behavior, deny-by-default action/frame gates and compatible central Avalonia/Grpc dependency constraints.",
      "bodyLength": 1094
    },
    {
      "id": "TR-ROMM-SEC-001",
      "body": "Public covers use an anonymous client; bearer auth is restricted to server-relative RomM cover paths. ROM filenames and resolved cache destinations are contained, downloaded through a temporary file, expected-size validated, and atomically published. Windows file-backed tokens use current-user DPAPI with atomic legacy-plaintext migration; unsupported operating systems fail closed.",
      "bodyLength": 383
    },
    {
      "id": "TR-VIC20-FLASH-001",
      "body": "Flash040Core exposes AdvanceCycles and the VIC-20 machine clock advances it. TYPE_B timeout/sector/chip budgets, busy reads, cancel, suspend, and resume are deterministic. Expansion-cart dirty payloads remain type-correct; host detach uses a same-directory temporary file and atomic replacement.",
      "bodyLength": 295
    },
    {
      "id": "TR-VIC20-PIXEL-001",
      "body": "Managed and xvic expose normal-border index/BGRA buffers at a common sync point. READY PAL/NTSC/busy index SequenceEqual is Exact-scoped. READY PAL, READY NTSC, and busy PAL native BGRA SequenceEqual vs xvic capture_visible_frame is also Exact-scoped (canvas RGB, opaque alpha; NTSC unpainted clamp rows opaque black). Other border modes remain Partial. Not whole-machine Exact.",
      "bodyLength": 378
    },
    {
      "id": "TR-VIC20-SOUND-001",
      "body": "Mos6561 owns one machine-agnostic Vic20Sound engine. System-clock advancement produces deterministic PCM16 mono and dispatches 256-sample batches without per-store allocation. Native parity is scoped to the covered silence and tone inputs.",
      "bodyLength": 239
    }
  ],
